<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs $36 mln Chile contract.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs $36 mln Chile contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Tuesday it had signed a contract with Startel to expand its D-AMPS network in Chile.</p>
<p>The contract, valued at $36 million, is the third expansion order this year with all three totalling $82 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The contract for the expansion of both capacity and coverage includes the latest Ericsson dual-mode (analogue/digital) RBS 884 base stations plus switching and services,&quot; Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>Startel, Chile's largest wireless network operator, has launched digital Personal Communication Services (PCS) based on the latest, most advanced D-AMPS IS-136 wireless standard, Ericsson said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
